WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.520
The Toothlight Treaty.

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:08.808
On Family Traditions Day, Lucia's class filled a wall with stories.

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:16.416
Some families brought songs. Some brought recipes, photographs, or tiny flags.

00:00:16.416 --> 00:00:23.952
When I was small in Madrid, I left my tooth beside a tiny mouse door. Perez always found it.

00:00:23.952 --> 00:00:29.520
And I left a note by the window. The Tooth Fairy always listened.

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:34.008
Lucia drew Papa's brick mouse door from Madrid.

00:00:34.008 --> 00:00:39.120
Beside it, she drew Mom's moonlit fairy window.

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:42.912
Which one is the real one?

00:00:42.912 --> 00:00:48.432
Lucia looked at the worksheet. It had only one little box.

00:00:48.432 --> 00:00:52.704
They are both real in my family.

00:00:52.704 --> 00:00:57.144
But the question followed her home like a pebble in her shoe.

00:00:57.144 --> 00:01:02.760
At merienda, her loose tooth wobbled with every careful bite.

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:06.072
Perez appreciates a brave tooth.

00:01:06.072 --> 00:01:10.008
The Tooth Fairy appreciates an honest note.

00:01:10.008 --> 00:01:14.760
The tooth popped free while Lucia was trying not to choose.

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:21.432
Papa opened his old coin box. Mom unfolded one of her childhood notes.

00:01:21.432 --> 00:01:26.400
What if choosing one leaves the other outside?

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:30.984
She drew both doors again on one folded page.

00:01:30.984 --> 00:01:37.560
Can both of you come? Please ask before deciding.

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:43.656
Behind the bakery wall, Ratoncito Perez checked his ledger twice.

00:01:43.656 --> 00:01:51.216
Enter quietly. Take respectfully. Leave the coin. Keep the local promise.

00:01:51.216 --> 00:01:56.304
Lucia's tooth lit one careful mark beside her name.

00:01:56.304 --> 00:02:01.224
Far away, the same question chimed in Tanda's satchel.

00:02:01.224 --> 00:02:07.992
Tanda followed the signal over rooftops until Madrid's mouse doors came into view.

00:02:07.992 --> 00:02:12.792
She landed at a brass door no taller than her hand.

00:02:12.792 --> 00:02:19.944
I received your invitation. But Madrid is not a branch office.

00:02:19.944 --> 00:02:25.728
Agreed. Lucia asked both of us to listen.

00:02:25.728 --> 00:02:28.416
May I enter?

00:02:28.416 --> 00:02:36.024
You may enter. You may listen. But you may not replace the road.

00:02:36.024 --> 00:02:41.424
Perez showed routes trusted by Madrid families for generations.

00:02:41.424 --> 00:02:51.360
Children leave teeth, notes, and tiny worries by our doors. We carry each one quietly home.

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:56.304
Big magic can make small doors disappear.

00:02:56.304 --> 00:03:03.000
And when Keepers work alone, a child's exact story can disappear between us.

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:12.384
They agreed on one thing: follow Lucia's signal. Perez chose the mouse roads. Tanda chose the sky.

00:03:12.384 --> 00:03:17.352
Perez snapped his ledger shut and bolted beneath Madrid.

00:03:17.352 --> 00:03:23.328
Tanda rose above the rooftops, keeping the same small light in sight.

00:03:23.328 --> 00:03:28.824
Brick road and moonlit window led to the same awake child.

00:03:28.824 --> 00:03:32.928
Perez came through the walls without waking the cat.

00:03:32.928 --> 00:03:37.152
Tanda waited at the window until Perez nodded.

00:03:37.152 --> 00:03:40.848
Each reached for the tooth—and stopped.

00:03:40.848 --> 00:03:46.752
Lucia was still awake, finishing the note she had written for both of them.

00:03:46.752 --> 00:03:53.784
I asked you both to come. I did not ask you to race.

00:03:53.784 --> 00:03:59.160
Papa's mouse door remembers where he came from.

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:04.224
Mom's note remembers that someone listened.

00:04:04.224 --> 00:04:09.240
My story needs room for my whole family.

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:15.024
Perez lowered his stamp. Tanda folded her wings close.

00:04:15.024 --> 00:04:20.856
My code protected the route, but not your whole story.

00:04:20.856 --> 00:04:26.904
And I followed the signal before asking what your family already trusted.

00:04:26.904 --> 00:04:33.768
Lucia turned her drawing over. The Treaty would begin in a child's own words.

00:04:33.768 --> 00:04:36.960
Ask the family.

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:44.256
Keep the exact story. Listen together before deciding.

00:04:44.256 --> 00:04:49.464
The words were Lucia's—not the fairy's and not the mouse's.

00:04:49.464 --> 00:04:54.072
Perez stamped the page without changing a single line.

00:04:54.072 --> 00:05:02.112
Tanda touched the edge. Lucia's complete memory closed safely inside its golden Toothlight.

00:05:02.112 --> 00:05:07.200
Perez carried the tooth through Madrid's trusted mouse roads.

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:12.720
Tanda carried Lucia's question so other Keepers could learn from it.

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:18.600
In the morning, Lucia added a second box to the class worksheet.

00:05:18.600 --> 00:05:23.544
My family has more than one true door.

00:05:23.544 --> 00:05:30.048
Her class saw the same drawing, now glowing as one complete Toothlight.

00:05:30.048 --> 00:05:40.080
And so the first Treaty joined mouse road to fairy sky—standing beside each tradition, so every family story could stay whole.
